{"t":1789859031,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"35839749-653f-459a-8fc4-8c68a26c8719","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-09-19T19:33:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 191933\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n333 PM EDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nCoastal Flood Advisory has been issued for Anne Arundel County.\n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Showers and possible thunderstorms return Sunday.\n\n- 2) Rain showers & cooler temperatures persist into midweek ahead of \n     drier conditions next weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers and possible thunderstorms return\nSunday.\n\nFair weather is expected through this evening. Low overcast\nconditions are expected to develop late this evening and through\nthe overnight as moisture advection develops atop a shallow cool\nlayer on SE winds. By daybreak, expect showers to move into\nwestern Maryland and track southeast across the area. A second\nround of afternoon showers is expected to move in from the\nAppalachian region and southern Pennsylvania. A few\nthunderstorms are possible along Interstate 64 in central\nVirginia, but severe wx appears unlikely. Showers will continue\ninto the evening along a frontal zone before dissipating or\nshifting south late Sunday night. \n\nLight rain or off and on showers will persist through Tue \nmorning, particularly along and west of the Blue Ridge Mountains\nin areas of onshore flow. Expect a noticeable cooling trend \nbeginning Monday in the wake of the cold front late Sunday \nnight. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Rain showers & cooler temperatures persist into \nmidweek ahead of drier conditions next weekend.\n\nMid-level moisture overhead will coincide with an area of low \npressure just off the East Coast tracking north on Wednesday. Weak \ninstability at the surface will suppress thunderstorm activity for \nthe most part, but expect rain showers to continue through Wednesday \nand Thursday as shortwave disturbances continue to track across\ntShowers and possible thunderstorms return Sunday.he Mid-\nAtlantic. High temperatures continue to range in the 60s as \nthese disturbances move through. \n\nAs the coastal low skirts the Mid-Atlantic coastline, winds will \nbe elevated Wednesday and Thursday with wind gusts between 20-30 MPH \npossible, especially along the Chesapeake Bay. Winds could \npotentially be higher over the waters, and this onshore flow \ncombined with stronger tidal influence could increase coastal flood \nrisk during this period. Refer to the coastal flooding section below \nfor more details. \n\nAs this system tracks north towards the end of the week, winds along \nthe coastline should gradually decrease. Mid-level dry air moves in \noverhead from the Midwest, which should lead to diminishing rainfall \npotential heading into the weekend. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /19Z SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\n\nLow overcast conditions/MVFR cigs are expected to develop late\nthis evening and continue through midday Sunday. Sunday will\nfeature two rounds of showers, one in the morning, and one in\nthe afternoon toward evening. Any thunderstorms would be\nconfined to KCHO. Monday and Tuesday will feature low overcast\nconditions with flight restrictions likely. \n\nIntermittent sub-VFR conditions could persist into Wednesday & \nThursday as scattered showers continue throughout the region. Gusty \nwinds between 20-25 knots are possible on Thursday. Winds flow from \nnortheasterly to northerly by Friday. \n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\n\nWinds will flirt with SCA across the Chesapeake Bay waters\nthrough Monday night. A more definite upward trend is seen\nstarting late Monday night through the middle of the week when\nadditional advisories will be needed. \n\nNorth to northeasterly Wind gusts remain elevated through Wednesday \nand Thursday as an area of low pressure remains off the East Coast. \nShowers & a couple of thunderstorms are possible over the waters \nduring this period. As this system begins to track north late in the \nweek, winds should begin to decrease heading into the weekend. \n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\n\nCoastal Flood Advisory has been issued for Anne Arundel County.\nCBOFS guidance seems like the only guidance performing well with\nthe elevated water levels and showing the rapid response due to\nthe onshore flow. \n\nOnshore flow will persist through at least the middle of next\nweek with water levels remaining elevated with minor coastal\nflooding expected at times of high tide. At this time, the risk\nof moderate coastal flooding seems low. \n\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Coastal Flood Advisory from 9 PM this evening to 5 AM EDT \n     Sunday for MDZ014.\nVA...None.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 1 AM EDT Sunday for ANZ534-537-543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...LFR/SRT\nAVIATION...LFR/SRT\nMARINE...LFR/SRT\n"},"forecast":{"t":1789858975,"days":{"2026-09-19":{"hi":null,"lo":69,"pop":10,"short":"Mostly Cloudy"},"2026-09-20":{"hi":86,"lo":65,"pop":66,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-21":{"hi":75,"lo":62,"pop":51,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-22":{"hi":69,"lo":58,"pop":53,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-23":{"hi":67,"lo":58,"pop":47,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-24":{"hi":67,"lo":55,"pop":31,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-25":{"hi":68,"lo":55,"pop":26,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-26":{"hi":72,"lo":null,"pop":15,"short":"Slight Chance Rain Showers"}}},"grid":{"t0":1789858800,"n":48,"ceil":[25000,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.